# Canonical header and cache policy for assets.guitard.ca.
#
# This file uses the Cloudflare Pages / Netlify _headers convention. Under the current GitHub Pages deployment the file is NOT interpreted at request time; runtime enforcement is performed by Cloudflare Response Header Transform rules (see DEPLOYMENT.md section 6). The file is retained as a version- controlled specification of intent and as a drop-in policy if hosting ever moves to Cloudflare Pages or Workers Assets.
#
# Two consequences of the current split:
#   1. Any change to the /* or /404.html blocks below that must reach production requires a matching change in the Cloudflare Transform rules. `validate-live.mjs` in .github/workflows/validate-live.yml compares live response headers against this specification and will flag drift on the next scheduled run.
#   2. Cache-Control rules for /css/*.css, /*.jpg, /*.png, /*.svg, /favicon.ico, and /robots.txt describe intent only. Production currently serves whatever GitHub Pages defaults to for those paths, because no Cloudflare Transform rule targets them today.

# Every published resource is intentionally usable across origins, including favicons, social previews, and the BIMI image retrieved by email clients.
/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'none'; script-src-attr 'none'; connect-src 'none'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

# Unknown asset addresses use the custom image-focused error document.
/404.html
  Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: max-age=600, no-transform
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-site
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

# Each deployment publishes its exact Git commit so production freshness can be monitored.
/deployment.json
  Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: max-age=600

# The error-page stylesheet uses a query-string version and the same four-hour browser lifetime currently delivered by production asset responses.
/css/*.css
  Content-Type: text/css; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: max-age=14400

# Image assets currently receive a uniform four-hour browser cache lifetime.
/*.jpg
  Content-Type: image/jpeg
  Cache-Control: max-age=14400

/*.png
  Content-Type: image/png
  Cache-Control: max-age=14400

/*.svg
  Content-Type: image/svg+xml
  Cache-Control: max-age=14400

/favicon.ico
  Content-Type: image/vnd.microsoft.icon
  Cache-Control: max-age=14400

# Public crawler instructions use the same live four-hour lifetime.
/robots.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: max-age=14400
